Let $k$ be a number field and $F/k$ a CM elliptic curve. Set $\mathcal O=\operatorname{End}_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}(F)$, $D=|\operatorname{disc}\mathcal O|$, and $d=[k:\mathbb Q]$. Then $$\label{eq:cm-bounds}
 D\ll d^4,\qquad h(j_F)\ll1+\sqrt D.$$ At any complex embedding, choose a reduced period basis $f,f\tau_F$ and put $y_F=\Im\tau_F$. Then $$\label{eq:b-index}
 b=[\Lambda_F:\mathcal O f]
   =\frac{\sqrt D}{2y_F}\in\mathbb Z_{>0},\qquad
 y_F\le\sqrt D/2,\qquad b\ll\sqrt D.$$

There is a polarized abelian threefold $(B,L)/k$, isogenous to $E^2\times F$, such that $$\label{eq:threefold-estimate}
 n^{4/3}\ll
 (b^2+1)d\,\max\{1,h_{\mathrm F}(B),\log\deg_L B\},$$ and $$\label{eq:B-height-degree}
 h_{\mathrm F}(B)\le2h_{\mathrm F}(E)+h_{\mathrm F}(F)+\log n,\qquad
 \deg_LB=6n^4uv,
 \quad u=\left\lceil y^2\right\rceil,\quad v=\left\lceil y\right\rceil.$$
